## 3. Added in this fork — third-party upstream source & reference implementations

Malbolge Unshackled: Unshackled.c
  * Matthias Lutter (https://github.com/Lutter/malbolge-unshackled)
  * License: CC0 1.0 Public Domain
  * Untouched upstream reference interpreter executed by Makefile step 252.

Malbolge Unshackled (fixed 20-trit parity verifier): Unshackled-20.c
  * Matthias Lutter (https://github.com/Lutter/malbolge-unshackled)
  * License: CC0 1.0 Public Domain
  * Untouched upstream reference interpreter; compiled by vendor/Makefile for
    out-of-band rotwidth-independence parity verification ONLY (not invoked by
    the main relay Makefile).

K (ngn/k): ngnk-b9eeb91e.tar.gz
  * https://codeberg.org/ngn/k (pinned commit b9eeb91e0343ef6029f59d55dd98f82667b9bd59)
  * License: AGPLv3 (complete upstream source archive including LICENSE;
    vendored because upstream archived the repository)

## 4. Added in this fork — minimal spec-complete esolang runners (MIT)
# Following mame/quine-relay's precedent for tiny esolangs lacking packaged
# Ubuntu interpreters (each implements the full language spec).

Underload: underload.rb
  * self-made, complete 8/8 Underload spec (https://esolangs.org/wiki/Underload)
  * License: MIT

Emmental: emmental.rb
  * self-made, complete 13/13 Emmental spec with lexical '!' capture, verified
    against Chris Pressey's catseye/Emmental (https://esolangs.org/wiki/Emmental)
  * License: MIT

/// (Slashes): slashes.rb
  * self-made, exact leftmost single-step substitution spec (with O(N) fast path
    for non-overlapping 1-byte patterns) (https://esolangs.org/wiki////)
  * License: MIT

Beatnik: beatnik.rb
  * self-made, complete Beatnik spec (halts strictly on score 17; scores <5 and
    >=18 are no-ops) (https://esolangs.org/wiki/Beatnik)
  * License: MIT
